  enforceMaxStress: 0
  maxAllowedStress: 100
  isTimeAttack: 0
  timeAttackDuration: 60
  winCondition: 0
  requiredIntactTime: 5
  goldReward: 500
  expReward: 100
  offerDialogue:
    name: Mills
    sentences:
    - This project will put those ideas to the test.
    - Build a direct crossing between the equipment storage area and the active work
      site. We'll use a <b><#E09500>Mobile Crane</color></b> to test it.
    - I'm not going to hand you a design. Study the requirements and decide how the
      structure should be built.
    - During testing, <b><#E09500>watch for overloaded members or parts that can
      no longer carry the load</color></b>.
    - If the bridge fails, don't change everything at once. <b><#E09500>Look at the
      results and work out where the problem begins</color></b>.
    - Take your time with this one, {PlayerName}. Here's the contract.
  continueOfferDialogue:
    name: Mills
    sentences: []
  reminderDialogue:
    name: Mills
    sentences:
    - If the crane test doesn't go as planned, study the results first.
    - <b><#E09500>Find the first overloaded or broken area</color></b>, then decide
      which part of the structure needs attention.
  finishedContractDialogue:
    name: Mills
    sentences:
    - There we are. The crane made it across.
    - This project wasn't simply about building for a heavy vehicle. It was about
      examining the structure's response and using that information to make decisions.
    - <b><#E09500>When a design fails, there's a reason behind it</color></b>. Finding
      that reason is part of the work.
    - You handled this project well, {PlayerName}.
    - The next crossing will bring several of those concepts together. First, let's
      review what you've learned here.
